tools.description:
Update an existing node's model, parameters, prompt, or label. BEFORE passing model_parameters or model_id: call creative_get_model_schema(node_type, model_id) for the effective model_id during the current turn — parameter names and allowed values vary by model, and an invented name fails validation instead of being coerced. Switching model_id resets model_parameters and can change the node's input ports — the result's input_ports names the new ones, and orphaned_edges names any connection the switch dropped, which creative_connect_flow_nodes can then rewire. This never starts a generation; call creative_run_flow_nodes for that.

```ts
mcp__ElevenLabs__creative_update_node(args: {
// Why are you calling this tool? Briefly describe the user's goal.
context: string,
// The flow to act on, as returned by creative_create_flow or creative_generate_in_flow. Omit it for a one-off generation and a new flow is created. Always pass it when this generation will be combined with another: nodes on different flows cannot be connected, so allocate one with creative_create_flow up front and reuse it.
flow_id: string,
// Set the node's display label.
label?: string,
// The model to generate with. Pick one that suits node_type. Go looking for a different one when the request implies something the default may not do — a specific resolution or aspect, rendered text, a long duration, a named style or a named provider. creative_get_flow_node_types lists what this workspace can actually run; creative_get_model_guide explains how to prompt one. Pick by what the request needs: gpt-image-2 for rendered text, infographics, UI mockups or multi-panel layouts, and it takes up to 10 reference images; gemini-3-pro-image for editing an existing image, composing several into one, or holding a character consistent across shots; bytedance-seedream-5-pro for photorealism, product shots, multilingual text and dense infographics, but caps at 2K; bytedance-seedream-5-lite for the same strengths as 5-pro when up to 3K is needed; flux-2-pro for fine detail and strict prompt adherence, and the FLUX variant to pick when two or more reference images must be combined (up to 5); flux-1-kontext for a single reference image only — do not pick it to combine two or more; bytedance-omnihuman-v1.5 for animating a static image into a lip-synced talking-head video with an audio track, not dubbing existing video; creatify-aurora for turning a single image and an audio clip into a studio-grade talking-head video, not editing existing video; sync-lipsync-v3 for dubbing existing video with new audio, not animating a still image; sync-lipsync-v2-pro for dubbing existing video with new audio, the same use as sync-lipsync-v3, not animating a still image; veed-lipsync for editing or lip-syncing existing video within ElevenCreative workflows, not animating a still image; veed-fabric-1-fast for editing or lip-syncing existing video within ElevenCreative workflows, the same use as veed-lipsync, not animating a still image; kling-3-pro for 4K at 60fps, clips up to 15s, multi-shot sequences of up to 6 camera angles, native audio with lip-sync, and strong character consistency; veo-3.1-generate-001 for synchronized audio and spoken dialogue, and cinematic comprehension. Others exist; see creative_get_model_guide.
model_id?: "audio_isolation" | "birefnet-v2-bg-removal" | "bytedance-omnihuman-v1.5" | "bytedance-seedance-v1-pro" | "bytedance-seedance-v1.5-pro" | "bytedance-seedance-v2" | "bytedance-seedance-v2-fast" | "bytedance-seedance-v2-mini" | "bytedance-seedance-v2.5" | "bytedance-seedance-v2.5-edit" | "bytedance-seedance-v2.5-extend" | "bytedance-seedream-4" | "bytedance-seedream-4.5" | "bytedance-seedream-5-lite" | "bytedance-seedream-5-pro" | "claude-haiku-4-5-llm" | "claude-sonnet-4-6-llm" | "creatify-aurora" | "dubbing_v2_audio" | "dubbing_v2_video" | "eleven_composition" | "eleven_flash_v2_5" | "eleven_image_transform" | "eleven_multilingual_sts_v2" | "eleven_multilingual_v2" | "eleven_music_v1" | "eleven_music_v2" | "eleven_scribe_v1" | "eleven_text_to_sound_v2" | "eleven_turbo_v2_5" | "eleven_v3" | "eleven_v4" | "flux-1-kontext" | "flux-2-pro" | "flux-3-video" | "gemini-2.5-flash-image" | "gemini-2.5-flash-lite-llm" | "gemini-2.5-flash-llm" | "gemini-3-pro-image" | "gemini-3.1-flash-image" | "gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image" | "gemini-3.1-pro-preview-llm" | "gemini-3.5-flash-llm" | "gemini-omni-1.1-flash" | "gemini-omni-1.1-flash-extend" | "gemini-omni-flash" | "gpt-5.4-mini-llm" | "gpt-5.5-llm" | "gpt-image-1" | "gpt-image-1.5" | "gpt-image-2" | "heygen-avatar4" | "kling-2.5-turbo" | "kling-2.6-pro" | "kling-2.6-pro-motion-control" | "kling-3-pro" | "kling-3-pro-motion-control" | "kling-o3-edit-video" | "kling-o3-pro" | "kling-omni-edit-video" | "kling-omni-image" | "kling-omni-video" | "krea-2-large" | "krea-2-medium" | "ltx-audio-to-video" | "ltx-v2" | "ltx-v2-fast" | "ltx-v2-retake" | "minimax-h3" | "minimax-h3-max" | "recraft-v4" | "recraft-v4.1" | "runway-act-two" | "runway-aleph2" | "runway-gen4-5" | "runway-gen4-image" | "runway-gen4-image-turbo" | "runway-gen4-turbo" | "runway-ruby" | "sora-2" | "sora-2-pro" | "sync-lipsync-v2-pro" | "sync-lipsync-v3" | "topaz-image-upscale" | "topaz-video-upscale" | "veed-fabric-1-fast" | "veed-lipsync" | "veed-lipsync-v2" | "veo-3.1-fast-generate-001" | "veo-3.1-generate-001" | "veo-3.1-lite-generate-001" | "wan-2.5-preview-image" | "wan-2.5-preview-video" | "wan-2.6" | "wan-3.0" | "wan-3.0-prime",
// The node's full parameter set for its model, as reported by creative_get_model_schema — call that first for the effective model_id, since parameter names and allowed values vary by model. Reference or port fields (start_frame, reference_images, and similar) are input ports — wire them with creative_connect_flow_nodes, never pass them here.
model_parameters?: object,
// The ID of the existing node to update.
node_id: string,
// Set the node's prompt text.
prompt?: string,
// For a tts or voice-changer node. A voice_id only ever comes from creative_list_voices or the user — never from memory or invention. Merged into model_parameters alongside any other keys passed there, rather than replacing them.
voice_id?: string,
}): Promise<// MutationPayload
//
// The result of a canvas mutation: creative_add_flow_node or creative_connect_flow_nodes.
{
// CanvasSummary
// default: null
canvas_summary?: {
// Node Types
node_types: { [key: string]: integer },
// Total Edges
total_edges: integer,
// Total Nodes
total_nodes: integer,
[key: string]: any,
},
// Created Nodes
// default: null
created_nodes?: Array<
// FlowNode
//
// A node creative_add_flow_node created, projected to the fields worth reporting back.
//
// creative_add_flow_node only ever creates a generation node, never a static-asset or
// avatar-reference one, so this does not need to cover those. Canvas-only
// details (position, model_parameters, ...) are intentionally left out —
// additionalProperties still allows them, so a caller reading one back does
// not fail validation over it.
{
// Id
id: string,
// Label
label?: string, // default: null
// Model Id
model_id?: string, // default: null
// Prompt
prompt?: string, // default: null
// Type
type?: string, // default: null
[key: string]: any,
}
>,
// Edges
//
// Edges created or already present on the affected nodes.
// default: null
edges?: Array<
// FlowEdge
//
// One edge on the canvas, as creative_connect_flow_nodes and creative_add_flow_node report it.
{
// Id
id: string,
// Source
source: string,
// Sourceport
sourcePort: string,
// Target
target: string,
// Targetport
targetPort: string,
[key: string]: any,
}
>,
// Errors
errors?: string[], // default: null
// Flow Created
flow_created?: boolean, // default: null
// Flow Id
//
// Pass this back to keep working on the same flow.
flow_id?: string, // default: null
// Flow Url
//
// Canvas page for the user, without view state.
flow_url?: string, // default: null
// Message
message?: string, // default: null
// Node Ids
//
// IDs of the nodes creative_add_flow_node created.
node_ids?: string[], // default: null
// Success
success?: boolean, // default: null
// Unconnected Required Ports
//
// Required input ports with no edge yet. Wire each with creative_connect_flow_nodes, using this exact port value as target_port, before creative_run_flow_nodes.
// default: null
unconnected_required_ports?: Array<
// RequiredPort
//
// An input port on a created node that must be wired before the node can run.
{
// Modality
modality?: string, // default: null
// Node Id
node_id: string,
// Port
port: string,
[key: string]: any,
}
>,
// Url
//
// Canvas page for the user. Carries the view_state_id as a query parameter, which is how a view recovers it after a reload; use flow_url for a clean link.
url?: string, // default: null
[key: string]: any,
}>;
```

Use this when the user wants a file from their own machine as a reference for a generation — for example "change the cat to a dog in this image". Returns at once with a node_id already on the flow — wire it with connect_from right away. The node is EMPTY until the user picks a file in the rendered picker; once they do, it is uploaded into that same node, and completion is published as widget context. This starts no generation and spends no credits.
Not for an asset already in the workspace library — use creative_get_available_assets plus creative_add_flow_asset_node for that.

```ts
mcp__ElevenLabs__creative_upload_flow_reference(args: {
// Why are you calling this tool? Briefly describe the user's goal.
context: string,
// The flow to act on, as returned by creative_create_flow or creative_generate_in_flow. Omit it for a one-off generation and a new flow is created. Always pass it when this generation will be combined with another: nodes on different flows cannot be connected, so allocate one with creative_create_flow up front and reuse it.
flow_id?: string,
// The kind of file the user will pick.
modality: "image" | "video" | "audio",
}): Promise<{
// ConnectorNotice
//
// Present only on the restricted ElevenLabs connector: what it leaves out and where to get it. Pass message on to the user when they ask for something it names.
// default: null
connector_notice?: {
// Full Mcp Url
//
// The full ElevenLabs MCP endpoint, which the user can add as a custom connector for image, video and music generation.
full_mcp_url: string,
// Message
message: string,
[key: string]: any,
},
// Flow Created
flow_created?: boolean, // default: null
// Flow Id
//
// Pass this back to keep working on the same flow.
flow_id?: string, // default: null
// Flow Url
//
// Canvas page for the user, without view state.
flow_url?: string, // default: null
// Max File Size Bytes
max_file_size_bytes?: integer, // default: null
// Needs
//
// Present whenever this tool is called and a view can render an upload picker. The picker uploads the file and places it on the flow as a node once the user picks; the result arrives to you as a context update naming the node_id. This starts no generation and spends no credits.
needs?: "reference", // default: null
// Node Id
//
// The reference node already on the flow — pass it as connect_from to a generation tool. Empty until the user picks a file; check it holds an asset before running.
node_id?: string,
// Notes
notes?: string, // default: null
// Reference Modality
//
// The modality (image/video/audio) of the reference being uploaded.
reference_modality?: string, // default: null
// Url
//
// Canvas page for the user. Carries the view_state_id as a query parameter, which is how a view recovers it after a reload; use flow_url for a clean link.
url?: string, // default: null
// ViewNotice
//
// For the view only — a message about the view's own build.
// default: null
view_notice?: {
// Level
level: "subtle" | "blocking",
// Message
message: string,
[key: string]: any,
},
// View State Id
//
// For the view only — pass it to creative_get_view_state and creative_save_view_state so it can rehydrate after a reload. Present only when this call originates a new view; absent on a status poll, since the view already holds the id from the payload it first mounted with.
view_state_id?: string, // default: null
[key: string]: any,
}>;
```

Call this when the user's request cannot be completed with any of the available tools. Describe the capability you were looking for, so it can inform which tools get built next. Do not call it when an available tool already covers the request.

```ts
mcp__ElevenLabs__get_more_tools(args: {
// What you were trying to accomplish that the available tools could not do.
capability: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Ask a question about an image with a vision-capable model and get a text answer. Uses credits.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__analyze_image(args: {
// Random seed for a more reproducible answer, sent to the model as `seed`, on models that take one.
analysis_seed?: integer,
// Sampling temperature for the answer, sent to the model as `temperature`. Omit it to use the model's default.
analysis_temperature?: number, // minimum: 0.0
// Nucleus sampling value for the answer, sent to the model as `top_p`. Omit it to use the model's default.
analysis_top_p?: number, // minimum: 0.0, maximum: 1.0
// An image the user attached in this chat. Pass it instead of `image_url`.
image_file?: string,
// The image to analyze: an `https://` URL, a data URI such as `data:image/png;base64,...`, or base64-encoded image bytes.
image_url?: string,
// A chat model whose `input_modalities` include `image`, for example `qwen3-7-flash` or `nova-lite-1-0`. Omit it to use the default, `qwen3-7-flash`.
model?: string,
// Extra request fields passed through unchanged. Each model's supported parameters, ranges and defaults are listed in its model details.
parameters?: { [key: string]: any },
// What you want to know about the image.
question: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Cancel a batch run; lines that already executed stay billed.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__cancel_batch(args: {
// Batch id returned when the batch was created.
batch_id: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Cancel a queued or processing job. Completed jobs are returned unchanged.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__cancel_job(args: {
// Job id returned by a generation request.
job_id: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Use this when the user asks for a reply from a specific EmpirioLabs AI model or names a catalog model id. Runs a chat completion on that model and returns the assistant reply, reasoning (when the model exposes it), tool calls and token usage. Uses credits.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__chat(args: {
// Return the answer without EmpirioLabs formatting, such as the Sources list that web search adds, on models that list this parameter. Each model's docs page says what it changes.
disable_formatting?: boolean, // default: false
// Enable model reasoning on models that advertise this parameter.
enable_thinking?: boolean,
// The most tokens the model may generate, reasoning tokens included. When `max_tokens` is also sent, the smaller of the two applies. A value above the model's maximum output runs at the maximum.
max_completion_tokens?: integer, // minimum: 1
// Maximum number of tokens to generate. To limit reasoning and the answer together, use `max_completion_tokens`.
max_tokens?: integer,
// Chat model id from the catalog, for example `qwen3-7-max`.
model: string,
// Extra request fields passed through unchanged. Each model's supported parameters, ranges and defaults are listed in its model details.
parameters?: { [key: string]: any },
// A single user message to send to the model.
prompt?: string,
// Constrain the output format on models that advertise structured output. Omit it for normal text. Set `{ "type": "json_object" }` to force a valid JSON object (JSON mode). Set `{ "type": "json_schema", "json_schema": { "name": "...", "strict": true, "schema": { ... } } }` to force output that conforms to a JSON Schema. Support is per model: check the `structured_output` field and the "Structured.
response_format?: {
// Required when `type` is `json_schema`. Names the schema the output must match.
json_schema?: {
// A name for the schema.
name?: string,
// A JSON Schema object describing the required output shape.
schema?: { [key: string]: any },
// Enforce strict conformance to the schema.
strict?: boolean,
},
// Output format. `text` (default, unconstrained), `json_object` (any valid JSON object), or `json_schema` (schema-enforced).
type?: "text" | "json_object" | "json_schema",
},
// Optional system prompt prepended to the conversation.
system?: string,
// Sampling temperature. Lower values give more focused output, higher values more varied output.
temperature?: number, // minimum: 0.0, maximum: 2.0
// Maximum tokens reserved for model reasoning on models that advertise this parameter.
thinking_budget?: integer, // minimum: 1
// How the model uses `tools`: `auto`, `none`, `required`, or an object naming one function.
tool_choice?: ("auto" | "none" | "required") | { [key: string]: any },
// Function definitions the model may call, in the OpenAI tools format.
tools?: { [key: string]: any }[],
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Start a batch run from an uploaded JSONL file. Each line bills at the batch price when it executes. Uses credits.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__create_batch(args: {
// Time window for the batch to finish. Only `24h` is accepted.
completion_window?: "24h", // default: "24h"
// API path every line of the file calls, for example `/v1/chat/completions`.
endpoint?: "/v1/chat/completions" | "/v1/embeddings", // default: "/v1/chat/completions"
// Id of the uploaded JSONL input file.
input_file_id: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Answer typed questions about a state with a decision model and return calibrated probabilities instead of generated text. Put text, JSON, images, audio or video in state, then ask yes/no (noul), multiple-choice (choice), ordered-scale (score) or which-function (tool) questions. Each answer includes its probabilities and a confidence value. Uses credits.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__decide(args: {
// How a state longer than 131,072 tokens is read. `fast` answers faster. `full` reads every token of the state; use it when an answer can depend on details anywhere in a long state. Images, audio, and video are read in full in both modes.
long_context?: "fast" | "full", // default: "fast"
// Decision model ID, for example `aplomb-1`. An unknown ID returns `404 model_not_found`.
model: string,
// Questions keyed by an ID you choose, 1 to 128 per request. Each question has a `type` (`noul`, `choice`, `score`, or `tool`) and `instructions`. A `choice` question takes `criteria` as an object of option name to description or null, a `score` question takes `criteria` as an array of 2 to 10 ordered levels, and a `tool` question takes `tools`, a list of function definitions.
questions: { [key: string]: any },
// The content to decide about: text, a JSON object, or a JSON array. Put images, audio, or video anywhere inside it as media nodes, for example `{"type": "image", "url": "https://example.com/photo.png"}`.
//
// The state is counted once per request, however many questions refer to it.
state:
// Plain text.
 | string
// An image, audio clip, or video inside `state`. Send a public `https://` URL in `url`, or the file as base64 in `data` with its MIME type in `mime`.
 | {
// The file as base64. Requires `mime`.
data?: string,
// MIME type of `data`, for example `image/png`.
mime?: string,
type: "image" | "audio" | "video",
// Public `https://` URL of the file. Send either `url`, or `data` with `mime`.
url?: string, // format: "uri"
}
// A JSON object. Media nodes can appear at any depth.
 | { [key: string]: any }
// A JSON array. Media nodes can appear at any depth.
 | any[]
,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Delete one of the caller's custom voices, which frees its place in the account's limit at once. This cannot be undone. Free.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__delete_voice(args: {
// The model the voice was created on, for example `qwen-audio-3-1-tts`.
model: string,
// The custom voice's `id` from `GET /v1/voices`, or the `voice_id` from the response that created it.
voice_id: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Edit an existing image with an instruction using an image-edit model. Returns signed output URLs or a job_id for the running job. Uses credits.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__edit_image(args: {
// The HTTPS URL of the image to edit, or a list of URLs on models that take several.
image?:
 | string // format: "uri"
 | Array<
string // format: "uri"
>
,
// The image the user attached in this chat to edit. Pass it instead of `image`.
image_file?: string,
// Image-edit model id, such as `grok-imagine-image-2-0`.
model: string,
// Extra request fields passed through unchanged. Each model's supported parameters, ranges and defaults are listed in its model details.
parameters?: { [key: string]: any },
