```

Create embedding vectors for one or more texts with an embedding model. Uses credits.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__embeddings(args: {
// Vector size, on models that offer more than one. A model with a fixed size returns `400` for any other value. See the model page for the sizes it offers.
dimensions?: integer, // minimum: 1
// Vector encoding: `float` arrays or `base64` strings of little-endian 32-bit floats. Both work on every embedding model.
encoding_format?: "float" | "base64", // default: "float"
// Text to embed, or an array of texts. Multimodal embedding models also take an array of `text`, `image`, and `video` parts. Token IDs return `400`.
input:
 | string
 | string[]
 | Array<
{
text?: string,
// `text`, `image`, or `video`.
type?: string,
// Public URL of the image or video.
url?: string,
[key: string]: any,
}
>
,
// On models that take one: an instruction describing the search task, set when embedding search queries and left out for documents. Its tokens bill as input.
instruct?: string,
// Embedding model id, for example `text-embedding-v4`.
model: string,
// On models that offer sparse vectors: `dense` returns the vector in `embedding`, `sparse` returns token weights in `sparse_embedding` with an empty `embedding`, and `dense_and_sparse` returns both. Every output type bills the same tokens.
output_type?: "dense" | "sparse" | "dense_and_sparse", // default: "dense"
// Extra request fields passed through unchanged. Each model's supported parameters, ranges and defaults are listed in its model details.
parameters?: { [key: string]: any },
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Fetch the full text of a search result by id (model:<slug> or doc:<page>).

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__fetch(args: {
// A result id: model:<slug> or doc:<page>.
id: string,
}): Promise<{ id: string, metadata?: { [key: string]: any }, text: string, title: string, url: string }>;
```

Generate a 3D asset with a 3D generation model from a text prompt, one or more images, or both, depending on the model. Returns a job_id for the running job. Uses credits.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__generate_3d(args: {
// Target face count of the simplified mesh.
decimation_target?: integer, // default: 500000, minimum: 10000, maximum: 1000000
// Reference image for image-to-3D generation.
image?:
 | string // format: "uri"
// Base64 data URI or inline image bytes.
 | string
,
// An image the user attached in this chat to turn into a 3D model. Pass it instead of `image`.
image_file?: string,
// Alias of `image` for a public URL, on models that accept it. Prefer `image`.
image_url?: string, // format: "uri"
// Several images of the same object, on models that accept more than one. Each item is a public URL or a base64 data URI. The model page gives the number of images the model accepts.
images?: string[],
// Maximum generation tokens.
max_num_tokens?: integer, // default: 49152, minimum: 1024, maximum: 131072
// 3D generation model id from list_models. Use `trellis-2-4b` for an image when the user names no model.
model: string,
// Extra request fields passed through unchanged. Each model's supported parameters, ranges and defaults are listed in its model details.
parameters?: { [key: string]: any },
// Text prompt, on models that accept one: a description of the object to generate, or guidance for a generation from images.
prompt?: string,
// Rebuild the mesh topology before export.
remesh?: boolean, // default: true
// Generation resolution. Higher values add detail and take longer.
resolution?: "512" | "1024" | "1536", // default: "1024"
// Return the asset as a `url` or as inline `b64_json`.
response_format?: "url" | "b64_json", // default: "url"
// Random seed for reproducible results.
seed?: integer, // default: 42, minimum: 0, maximum: 2147483647
// Texture size in pixels.
texture_size?: "1024" | "2048" | "4096", // default: "2048"
// Seconds to wait for the result before returning a job_id for the running job (default 40, max 50).
wait_seconds?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 50
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Generate music or sound effects from a prompt with an audio generation model (for example ace-step-1-5-xl). Returns a signed URL or a job_id for the running job. Uses credits.

```ts
mcp__EmpirioLabs_AI__generate_audio(args: {
// Prompt adherence. Higher = closer to prompt but less creative.
cfg_scale?: number,
// Output length in seconds, on models that take it. Some models name it `audio_duration`; see the model page.
duration?: number,
// Song lyrics, on models that sing them.
lyrics?: string,
// Music or sound model id from list_models. Use `ace-step-1-5-xl` for music when the user names no model.
model: string,
// Audio file format.
output_format?: "mp3" | "wav" | "flac" | "ogg",
// Extra request fields passed through unchanged. Each model's supported parameters, ranges and defaults are listed in its model details.
parameters?: { [key: string]: any },
// Natural-language description of the audio to generate.
prompt?: string,
// Random seed for reproducibility.
seed?: integer,
