Builds a Weave workflow: creates one and/or applies a batch of node and edge additions, node duplications, edits and removals to its graph. Pass `createNew: true` (optionally with `name`) to start a new workflow, or `workflowId` to build into an existing one. Get the `nodeTypeId`s you need from weave_get_node_catalog first. Creating and populating a workflow in one call is the normal path; batch as much of a build as you can rather than making many small calls. Continue a build with the `workflowId` from the response; never create a second workflow to work around a missing id. A batch applies partially: fix and resend only what was skipped or ignored. Re-read the workflow only when the reply says to. Running a workflow is not supported here: say so, and give its Weave editor link from weave_get_workflow. If it has a tool, offer to run the tool instead (same id) and call weave_run_tool only if the user agrees. To run it from here later, the user can create a tool from it in the editor (https://help.weavy.ai/en/articles/12267755-tools). If it has no tool, you may offer to run its models one by one with weave_run_model, saying plainly that this is not running the workflow: only its model nodes run this way, so steps like crops, compositing and exports are skipped and nothing is saved back to the workflow, so results will differ. Never say you ran the workflow.

