Copy an authorized raw-byte conversation, personal Library, or Project-backed file into the model's working container for programmatic use. For Project-backed files, use raw_file only; uploaded Project files and Library-backed Project files can succeed when their current backing bytes and Project access are still available. Connector-synced Project docs and retrieval-only Project knowledge cannot be materialized because indexed text does not prove an exportable original file. Google Drive-backed Project docs support files.search, files.find, and files.read for indexed content, but requests for current content, downloads, exports, PDF creation, or local/working copies require an available live Google Drive connector and either an exact Drive URL or file ID supplied by the user or a verified cloud_doc_url from Project source metadata. A Project Files file_id is not a Drive file ID. If the live connector is unavailable, explain that live Drive access is unavailable. If exact Drive identity is unavailable, ask for the exact Drive link or file ID; do not search Drive broadly by title or fall back to Project snapshot bytes. Prefer files.search, files.find, or files.read when a container copy is unnecessary.

