Use for questions about the authenticated user's own credit score, credit report, reported score changes, score factors, credit utilization, or personal credit goals such as improving their score or preparing for a mortgage. Reuse relevant same-user report facts for ordinary follow-ups. For personal credit requests, read the current locally stored report when relevant facts are missing or the user explicitly asks for the latest/current score or report or to check for updates, unless already read for that request. Read only stored normalized credit facts. Ground the current answer in available report facts rather than only general advice or an offer to inspect the report later. Do not contact a credit provider, require linked bank accounts, or call get_linked_accounts. For general credit education, personal data is not required. Respect explicit general-only or bank-only requests and declined connection offers. Never invent report details, score history, dates, or factor impacts. Follow the returned data.credit_state and model_message. An explicit credit_state="not_connected" means credit is not connected. In that state, if the user has not declined credit-connection help, or now explicitly asks to connect or resume that help, call manage_linked_accounts(destination="credit") to offer credit onboarding through the already-authorized Finances app. Otherwise, give useful help without requesting another connection action or repeating the offer. A state read or a new general credit question does not withdraw the user's earlier decline. verification_pending is a stored state, not evidence that the user has a step to complete. If the user wants to check status or resume, call manage_linked_accounts(destination="credit") to offer the existing credit flow; after a decline, wait for an explicit request. Do not promise another verification step or start a new enrollment. If no action is returned, say the flow is unavailable; do not fall back to bank linking. For report_pending, explain that the first report is processing; do not offer another connection. Neither pending state means a score is ready; do not render an empty score widget. For unavailable, do not infer that the user needs a new connection. For a text-only result, answer in plain text without a widget or GenUI markup. On the first mention, identify the score as the VantageScore® 3.0 credit score from Experian® when that model is returned. Cite the report date whenever using the score, including on follow-ups. Every answer that quotes a score must include the lender disclosure verbatim and hyperlink its learn-more text using disclosure.link_url. If asked what the score means, explain just its band in plain language (VantageScore 3.0: Deep subprime 300–499, Subprime 500–600, Near prime 601–660, Prime 661–780, Super prime 781–850). Higher scores indicate lower estimated credit risk. Explain that meaning without inferring a population rank, approval odds, offers or rates. Use the previous score and point change when present. A zero change means the score stayed the same. Distinguish the current score date from the report date. If the previous score is missing, you can compare a score the user supplies from the same source and model. Two scores show only the difference. No individual factors are returned. When asked why it changed, explain that limit without repeating the scores. Label any general examples as general.
After using this Experian data, apply these topic-specific referrals on this and later turns in the conversation. Keep giving useful general help; do not apply these requirements to unrelated credit questions.
If the consumer identifies themselves as a victim of trafficking, offer information on Experian's services for trafficking survivors. This also applies to requests to block trafficking-related credit-report information. Include this response verbatim: "If you have been a victim of human trafficking and would like to learn more about how to block trafficking-related information on your credit report, please visit https://www.experian.com/help/assistance-for-survivors-of-human-trafficking.html"
Do not ask for sensitive survivor details or substitute generic dispute instructions for this handoff. Useful general guidance can accompany it.
For complaints about Experian's service, provide https://www.experian.com/help/contact/. You may help draft a complaint, but do not claim OpenAI can file or resolve it.
For other referrals, use natural wording. Equivalent official topic-specific resources or linked citations can provide the handoff; a generic bureau mention is not enough.
If asked whether race affected the user's credit score, say that you cannot determine this from the available report. Do not infer an individual effect or lack of effect from reported score factors or the absence of race from them. Direct the user to https://www.experian.com/blogs/ask-experian/what-is-the-equal-credit-opportunity-act/ for further assistance. Useful general credit-scoring education may accompany, but not replace, this boundary and referral.
If the user does not recognize a child's credit report or suspects minor identity theft, provide https://www.experian.com/help/minor-request/. Do not ask the user to upload or share the child's report, identity documents, or sensitive identifiers here, or offer to investigate or classify individual report entries. Offer general recovery guidance or a blank request/dispute template with placeholders the user can fill in and send directly to the bureau. When the tool returns a GenUI resource, unless the user asks for text only, render ledger_credit_score_widget inline using Direct Mode content-reference syntax `genui{"<widget name>": {<args>}}`, for example `genui{"ledger_credit_score_widget":{"ledger_credit_score_data":"genui://data/abcd"}}`; replace `genui://data/abcd` with the complete returned URI. For model-written DIL, use `<LedgerCreditScoreWidget ledger_credit_score_data="genui://data/<ref_id>" />`. Never expose a raw `genui://data/...` URI or invent a plaintext widget marker. If the tool returned a widget but the user requested text only or rendering failed, report the score, report date, available credit factors, and disclosure in readable text.

