Run capabilities of Alexandria data providers and return their typed, sourced records: one, or up to ten in one call when a task needs several lookups. Alexandria is Firecrawl's library of data providers across companies, people, jobs, finance and filings, public records and government spending, real estate, places and restaurants, retail and prices, package registries and developer data, news, research, and more. For people and company enrichment or search, use people_company_enrich or people_company_search when they are listed, and for job postings use jobs_search when it is listed; call a provider here directly only when the user asks for that provider. Each entry of `calls` is {provider, capability, options}: `provider` and `capability` come from firecrawl_search results or alexandria_library_search, and `options` follow the capability's contract, which marks required inputs and any requiresOneOf groups (at least one member per group). Where the contract declares pagination, its fields page through results with the same filters. Returns one result per call, in the same order, in data.alexandria, each with data, records, or an error with a code; one call can fail while the others succeed, and an invalid call returns an error naming the valid options. A result too large to return inline is retained, and nextTool reads it in slices. Billed per executed capability; discovery is free. Some providers require accepted terms; when a response reports a terms requirement, direct the user to the Firecrawl dashboard URL in that response.

