Create or change one of the user's team skills: instructions an agent follows, naming capabilities as @provider/capability. Without id, creates one: write name, description and body, or copy a skill under /library/skills with from (its id: <id> for /library/skills/firecrawl/<id>, team:<slug> for /library/skills/team/<slug>); fields you also give override the copy, and a library skill copies its SKILL.md only. The new skill is enabled and listed in /library/skills/INDEX as /library/skills/team/<slug>; a taken slug is a conflict. With id (team:<slug>) and baseVersion, the version: in its SKILL.md, changes its name, description or body (a new version), or whether it is enabled or listed; a skill changed since is refused with conflict, so read it again and reapply. A body edited from the text you read must write each capability as @provider/capability again: the plain code it shows saves no reference. Library skills cannot be changed; copy one. Skills cannot be deleted here. Returns the saved skill's path and the command that reads it. Save only what the user asked for. Free.

