Find job postings and check whether a posting is still open. Use it to: find jobs by role and place (query, with location, remote or posted_within_days); read one posting by url and tell whether it is still open; check up to 10 posting urls in one call; list a company's open roles from its own job board (company, a name or domain; add query for one role there); and see who is hiring for a role (query with group_by "employer"). Every row has the same normalized fields: title, company, location, remote, posted_at as the board states it, url, source, a status, and checked_at, the time Firecrawl read it. status is open when the posting was read from the employer's board or live posting page in this call, and unverified when it comes from a job site and was not confirmed on the employer's board. A posting checked by url can also be closed, not_found or error. A single url returns the full description; list rows carry it with include_description. A company search names the boards it read and what each covers; when no board is found, rows come from job sites and notes says so. boards_only searches employers' own boards only. Each provider read is charged its listed price; max_credits caps the call. Example: {"query":"data engineer","location":"Berlin","posted_within_days":14}.

