Find people or companies you don't know yet, by filters. Not for someone you can already name: for a named person (with their company or domain, a LinkedIn URL or an email) or a named company, call people_company_enrich instead; a request naming one person is refused and pointed there. Set entity to "person" or "company" and give filters: people by title, seniority, function, employer and location; companies by industry, headcount, location, technology, keywords or founding year. Firecrawl asks its search providers one at a time, cheapest first, and only those that apply every filter given. When none does, it searches companies first and then people at those companies; a request no provider or chain covers is refused naming the filter to drop. With company_domains the search stops at the first provider that finds anyone; otherwise it fills limit across up to three providers. Rows carry name, title, company, location and LinkedIn URL, never emails or phones: use people_company_enrich for contact details. Each provider call is charged its listed price; max_credits caps the call. Example: {"entity":"person","filters":{"titles":["Head of Data"],"company_domains":["example.com"]},"limit":10}.

